<header class="page-hero reveal">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Leafix GHY</a> / Kalapahar Guide</p>
    <h1>Kalapahar, Guwahati.<br>A neighbourhood guide.</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">Not a tourist area. That's the point. Kalapahar is old Guwahati — hilly, residential, with trees, lanes and a pace that central Guwahati doesn't have. This is where Leafix GHY is.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="funnel-section reveal">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">The area</span>
    <h2 class="funnel-headline">A hill neighbourhood that feels like it hasn't rushed.</h2>
    <p class="funnel-body">Kalapahar sits between the main commercial corridors of Guwahati without being part of them. Streets narrow quickly. Auto-rickshaws are the default way around. There's a morning market. There are temples tucked between buildings. Older homes with large gardens sit next to newer construction.</p>
    <p class="funnel-body">It's a genuinely residential area — not a guest-house strip, not a hotel zone. People live here. That means it's quieter, more local, and has the kind of neighbourhood rhythm that commercial areas don't.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="funnel-section reveal" style="background: var(--surface);">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Around the neighbourhood</span>
    <h2 class="funnel-headline">What you'll find in and around Kalapahar.</h2>
    <div class="guide-grid">
      <div class="guide-card">
        <p class="guide-card-label">Food &amp; chai</p>
        <h3>Local dhabas and chai stalls</h3>
        <p>Within walking distance there are a few small dhabas serving Assamese staples — dal, rice, pork, fish. Chai stalls open early. Not Instagram spots — actual food.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-card">
        <p class="guide-card-label">Morning</p>
        <h3>Small neighbourhood market</h3>
        <p>A local market a short walk away sells vegetables, fruits and basic supplies in the morning. Good for stocking the kitchen if you're on a longer stay.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-card">
        <p class="guide-card-label">Green</p>
        <h3>Trees and walking lanes</h3>
        <p>More tree cover than most parts of central Guwahati. Some lanes are suitable for an evening walk without worrying about traffic.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-card">
        <p class="guide-card-label">Getting around</p>
        <h3>Autos and Ola/Uber</h3>
        <p>Shared autos run on the main routes nearby. Ola and Uber are available and affordable. Autos are better for short hops — cabs for anything longer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-card">
        <p class="guide-card-label">Necessities</p>
        <h3>Pharmacy &amp; ATM nearby</h3>
        <p>A pharmacy is roughly 5 minutes' walk. ATMs and basic shops are within easy reach of the main lane.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-card">
        <p class="guide-card-label">Feel</p>
        <h3>Quiet by night</h3>
        <p>Not a nightlife area. Quiet by 10pm. If you're coming to rest and work, that's exactly what this neighbourhood is for.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="funnel-section reveal">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Distances from Kalapahar</span>
    <h2 class="funnel-headline">Where things are relative to where you'll be staying.</h2>
    <div style="max-width: 560px; margin-top: 32px;">
      <div class="distance-row"><span>Guwahati Railway Station</span><span>~15 min</span></div>
      <div class="distance-row"><span>Gauhati Medical College (GMC)</span><span>~15 min</span></div>
      <div class="distance-row"><span>Uzan Bazar riverfront</span><span>~12 min</span></div>
      <div class="distance-row"><span>Fancy Bazaar market</span><span>~15 min</span></div>
      <div class="distance-row"><span>Kamakhya Temple</span><span>~20–25 min</span></div>
      <div class="distance-row"><span>Guwahati Airport (LGB)</span><span>~25–30 min</span></div>
      <div class="distance-row"><span>Dispur (state capital area)</span><span>~20 min</span></div>
      <div class="distance-row"><span>Brahmaputra Ghat</span><span>~15 min</span></div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size: 0.84rem; opacity: 0.55; margin-top: 16px;">Times are approximate and traffic-dependent. Guwahati traffic can be heavy during peak hours (8–10am, 5–7pm).</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="funnel-section reveal" style="background: var(--dark-block); color: var(--bg);">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--amber);">Uzan Bazar vs Kalapahar</span>
    <h2 class="funnel-headline" style="color: var(--bg);">Considering where to stay in Guwahati?</h2>
    <p class="funnel-body" style="color: var(--bg); opacity: 0.82;">Uzan Bazar is older, more commercial, and closer to the Brahmaputra riverfront — lots of food options and activity. Kalapahar is quieter, more residential, and better suited to anyone who needs to sleep well, work from the apartment, or recover. They're about 12 minutes apart. <a href="/uzan-bazar-vs-kalapahar.html" style="color: var(--amber);">Full comparison →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="funnel-section reveal">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">Common questions</span>
    <h2 class="funnel-headline">Things people ask about Kalapahar before visiting.</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <p class="faq-q">Is Kalapahar a good area to stay in Guwahati?</p>
        <p class="faq-a">For anyone who wants quiet and a neighbourhood feel — yes. It's not a sightseeing area or a food-and-nightlife corridor. It's residential, centrally located, and easy to get out of when you need to explore.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <p class="faq-q">Is Kalapahar safe at night?</p>
        <p class="faq-a">Yes. Residential area — families, long-term residents. Not a market zone with late-night crowds. Quiet from around 10pm.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <p class="faq-q">How far is Kalapahar from Guwahati Railway Station?</p>
        <p class="faq-a">Approximately 15 minutes by auto or cab. Guwahati Airport is 25–30 minutes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <p class="faq-q">Is Kamakhya Temple nearby?</p>
        <p class="faq-a">About 20–25 minutes by cab. Go early morning on weekdays to avoid the longest queues.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

